	set_cmt	(0X19732,	"One of UseItem's item-type handlers (selected by word_2E410 bit 0x400). Sub-dispatches on the current SelectItemUseRecord's own es:[si+0x10] flags. Bit 2: pays a BCD material cost (0x94B3 vs a threshold at 0x512A, 'not enough' message if short) then sets a per-character flag via SetRecordFlag_10C using the item's own +0x1A field as the index -- same pattern as sub_1BBED's type-2 branch. Bit 0x200: builds a message string instead, no BCD cost -- plausibly a non-consuming 'read/examine' path.",	0);
